  "revisionReason": "EX-I7 remaining parameters batch 2 (2026-08-13 controlled tests on the actual 4.3.5 binary, synthetic read-only schema): --date-value-format and --datetime-value-format produced observable MYSQL-mode CSV changes and are ENABLED only for MYSQL-compatible CSV/CUT data; --partition produced the expected partition row counts and --exclude-data-types removed the tested decimal column, so both are ENABLED. The remaining time/timestamp/TZ/LTZ/NLS formats were only accepted without an applicable source column or still require Oracle-mode validation, so they remain VALIDATION_GATED. --enable-hidden-pk remains VALIDATION_GATED until table-structure, version and permission prechecks exist. --add-extra-message remains VALIDATION_GATED because CSV acceptance did not exercise its DDL behavior or bind current sys-credential permission facts. --year-value-format is absent from both the official documentation and the 4.3.5 binary and is not introduced; --preserve-zero-datetime remains untested and gated. Override correction: -t is the short option of --tenant, not --table, so the v6 shortName override is revoked in v7.",
